{"text": "DEPARTMENT OF THE NAVY\nCOMMANDER NAVAL AIR FORCE\nU.S. PACIFIC FLEET\nBOX 357051\nSAN DIEGO CALIFORNIA 92135-7051\n\n5720\nSer NO1J/045\n7 Jun 19\n\nOutline Editorial\nDON-NAVY-2019-006480\n\nDear Ladies and Gentlemen:\n\nThis letter is in response to your Freedom of Information Act (FOIA) request dated April 2,\n2019, wherein you requested the \u201cfiles, correspondence, and records generated between May 1,\n2002 and May 1, 2004, concerning the production and installation of the \"Mission\nAccomplished\" banner seen behind President George W. Bush during his May 1, 2003 speech\naboard the USS ABRAHAM LINCOLN.\u201d Your request was received in this office and has been\nprocessed under FOIA, 5 U.S.C. \u00a7552, and has been given FOIA #2019-006480.\n\nWe were unable to locate documentation pertaining to the production and installation of the\naforementioned \u201cMission Accomplished\u201d banner; however, we have enclosed pictures that were\ntaken aboard during President Bush\u2019s visit. Our search consisted of records that were maintained\nby USS ABRAHAM LINCOLN (CVN 72), but none were found.\n\nIf you are not satisfied with the response to this request, you may contact our office at the\ntelephone number and e-mail address provided below, as well as the Navy's FOIA Public\nLiaison, Mr. Christopher Julka, at christopher.a.julka@navy.mil;\nDONFOIAPublicLiaison@navy.mil or (703) 697-0031, for any further assistance and to discuss\nany aspect of your request. Additionally, you may contact the Office of Government\nInformation Services (OGIS) at the National Archives and Records Administration to inquire\nabout the FOIA mediation services they offer. The contact information for OGIS is as follows:\nOffice of Government Information Services, National Archives and Records Administration,\n8601 Adelphi Road-OGIS, College Park, Maryland 20740-6001, e-mail at ogis@nara.gov;\ntelephone at (202) 741-5770; toll free at 1-877-684-6448; or facsimile at (202) 741-5769.\n\nYou are also advised you have the right to appeal this determination through FOIA Online or\nin writing to the designee of the Secretary of the Navy under the above statute. An appeal,\nshould you choose to submit one, should be addressed to:\n\nOffice of the Judge Advocate General (Code 14)\n1322 Patterson Ave., S.E.\nSuite 3000\nWashington, DC 20374-5066\nTelephone: (202) 685-5450\nFax: (202) 685-5472\n\nFOR OFFICIAL USE ONLY \u2014 PRIVACY SENSITIVE",
